{"node_id": "real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small_9_HY_008", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0013"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0013_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "ADHD is diagnosed based on a person's symptoms, history,\nand behavior. If you or your child are experiencing symptoms\nof ADHD, the first step is to speak with a health care provider.", "semantic_text": "ADHD is diagnosed based on a person's symptoms, history, and behavior. If you or your child are experiencing symptoms of ADHD, the first step is to speak with a health care provider.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0013_geometry", "bbox": [614, 149, 1128, 232], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0013"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_32/hybrid/real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small/page_0009/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small_9_HY_009", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0014"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0014_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "The provider will want to know about the symptoms, including\nwhen they started, how severe they are, and how they impact aspects\nof life such as work, school, relationships, and daily functioning.", "semantic_text": "The provider will want to know about the symptoms, including when they started, how severe they are, and how they impact aspects of life such as work, school, relationships, and daily functioning.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0014_geometry", "bbox": [613, 234, 1188, 316], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0014"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_32/hybrid/real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small/page_0009/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small_9_HY_010", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0015"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0015_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "They'll also look for other possible causes. For example, certain\nmedical conditions and other mental health conditions, as well\nas nonmedical situations and experiences (such as a sudden life\nchange, trauma, or an ongoing stressor), can trigger symptoms that\nlook a lot like ADHD.", "semantic_text": "They'll also look for other possible causes. For example, certain medical conditions and other mental health conditions, as well as nonmedical situations and experiences (such as a sudden life change, trauma, or an ongoing stressor), can trigger symptoms that look a lot like ADHD.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0015_geometry", "bbox": [613, 317, 1170, 456], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0015"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_32/hybrid/real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small/page_0009/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small_9_HY_011", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0017"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0017_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "ADHD treatment typically involves a combination of medication,\ntherapy, and lifestyle modification or skills training.", "semantic_text": "ADHD treatment typically involves a combination of medication, therapy, and lifestyle modification or skills training.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0017_geometry", "bbox": [613, 505, 1155, 560], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0017"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_32/hybrid/real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small/page_0009/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small_9_HY_012", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0018"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0018_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "■ Medication can help improve focus and attention in people with\nADHD. Stimulants are prescribed most often, but there are also\nnonstimulant options available. Medication is an effective tool for\nmany people with ADHD, but it can come with side effects, and it\nmay take time to find the right one.\n■ Therapy can help people learn strategies and techniques to manage\nADHD symptoms and improve their overall functioning. It can help\nwith organization, time management, and problem-solving.\n■ Lifestyle modifications , including getting regular exercise,\neating nutritious and balanced meals, and getting plenty of sleep,\ncan help manage ADHD. Developing routines and schedules,\nsetting goals, and seeking support from family, friends, and\nsupport groups are also important.", "semantic_text": "■ Medication can help improve focus and attention in people with ADHD. Stimulants are prescribed most often, but there are also nonstimulant options available. Medication is an effective tool for many people with ADHD, but it can come with side effects, and it may take time to find the right one. ■ Therapy can help people learn strategies and techniques to manage ADHD symptoms and improve their overall functioning. It can help with organization, time management, and problem-solving. ■ Lifestyle modifications , including getting regular exercise, eating nutritious and balanced meals, and getting plenty of sleep, can help manage ADHD. Developing routines and schedules, setting goals, and seeking support from family, friends, and support groups are also important.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0018_geometry", "bbox": [628, 563, 1192, 911], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0018"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_32/hybrid/real_061_batch_56_Volume18_Issue4-508C-small/page_0009/decisions.json"}
